      "rationale": "This guarded equation defines decimalToBinarySpec for nonnegative integers by framing the base-two digit summary with the required db prefix and suffix.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-ed8bbd309f359712e14b367074db45188fe24eaf8c4627ee880a9f79a085944d",
      "start_line": 11,
      "text": "  rule decimalToBinarySpec(I)\n    => \"db\" +String binDigits(I) +String \"db\"\n    requires I >=Int 0"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 16,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "a6053be073dfd18cdaa5f54e44324cf4a4b209cc24dc48ad172447920b03637f",
      "rationale": "This guarded equation defines the negative-integer branch of decimalToBinarySpec, including the payload produced after slicing Python's negative binary rendering.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-a6053be073dfd18cdaa5f54e44324cf4a4b209cc24dc48ad172447920b03637f",
      "start_line": 14,
      "text": "  rule decimalToBinarySpec(I)\n    => (\"db\" +String (\"b\" +String binDigits(0 -Int I))) +String \"db\"\n    requires I <Int 0"
    }
  ],
